  "content": {
    "title": "What time is Selection Sunday for NCAA Tournament bracket reveal?",
    "text": "March 14, 2026Updated March 15, 2026, 5:56 p.m. ETFollow Selection Sunday live with USA TODAY Sports' live blog as the bracket is revealed.The anticipation is almost over.The full brackets both the Men's NCAA Tournament and Women's NCAA Tournament will be revealed Sunday. That will give fans ample time to fill out their brackets ahead of the First Four games.Most of the conference tournament games are now finished for both sides, with a few championship games scheduled for later today, Sunday, March 15, ahead of the reveal show for the men's and the women's 68-team fields.Duke, Michigan, and Arizona seem locked in as the No. 1 seeds on the men's side while Connecticut, UCLA, South Carolina and Texas seem to be the locks for the same on the women's side.For curious fans, here's what you need to know about Selection Sunday for the men's and women's NCAA tournaments, including show start times, TV channel, streaming information and more:Watch 2026 NCAA Tournament Selection Sunday shows live with Fubo (free trial)What time is Selection Sunday? When is March Madness bracket released?Men's Tournament selection show time: 6 p.m. ETWomen's Tournament selection show time: 8 p.m. ETThere will be two separate reveal shows for the men's and women's tournaments. The 68-team field for the men's side will be revealed at 6 p.m. ET on Sunday, with the assumption that no outstanding conference championship games remain.Following the men's reveal, the women's 68-team field will be announced shortly after, with a scheduled airing of 8 p.m. ET.What channel is Selection Sunday show?TV channels: CBS (men) | ESPN (women's)Streaming options: ESPN app | Fubo (free trial)The men's NCAA Tournament Selection Sunday show will be revealed live on CBS, while the women's bracket reveal will be broadcast on ESPN.Both bracket reveal shows can be streamed on Fubo, which not only carries CBS and the ESPN family of networks, but also offers a free trial to new subscribers.Watch 2026 NCAA Tournament Selection Sunday shows live with Fubo (free trial)Full men's March Madness schedule 2026Start date: Tuesday, March 17 (First Four)End date: Monday, April 7 (national championship)March Madness officially kicks off with the NCAA Tournament games, with the First Four round on Tuesday, March 17, at UD Arena in Dayton, Ohio.The Final Four will start on Saturday, April 4, at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis, with the national championship game on Monday, April 6.Here is the full schedule breakdown for the 2026 men's NCAA Tournament:First Four: Tuesday, March 17 and Wednesday, March 18First round: Thursday, March 19 and Friday, March 20Second round: Saturday, March 21 and Sunday, March 22Sweet 16: Thursday, March 26 and Friday, March 27Elite Eight: Saturday, March 28 and Sunday, March 29Final Four: Saturday, April 4National championship game: Monday, April 6Full women's March Madness schedule 2026Start date: Wednesday, March 18 (First Four)End date: Sunday, April 5 (national championship)Just like the men's side, the women's tournament begins with the First Four, with games beginning on Wednesday, March 18.The Final Four is scheduled to begin on Friday, April 3, in Phoenix at the Mortgage Matchup Center, with the national championship game two days later on Sunday, April 5.Here is the full schedule breakdown for the 2026 women's NCAA Tournament:First Four: Wednesday, March 18 andThursday, March 19Round of 64: Friday, March 20 and Saturday, March 21Round of 32: Sunday, March 22 and Monday, March 23Sweet 16: Friday, March 27 and Saturday, March 28Elite Eight: Sunday, March 29 and Monday, March 30Final Four: Friday, April 4National championship game: Sunday, April 6",
